from pathlib import Path
p=Path('history.js')
s=p.read_text()
old='''rankings:{title:"RANKING RULES",body:`<p>Participation in rankings is optional. Results remain private unless the player chooses <strong>INCLUDE ME IN RANKINGS</strong> in Personal Settings.</p><p>Only players who have opted into rankings are included. Ranking participants can see the ranking information of other ranking participants.</p><p><strong>Ranking participation does not affect your chances of winning.</strong> Choosing to appear in the rankings, or choosing to keep your results private, has no influence on your eligibility or chances of becoming a weekly or monthly winner. Quiz results are taken into account for winner selection regardless of the ranking privacy setting.</p><p>Players are ordered first by the number of correct answers and then by the number of different days played during the relevant period. Players with the same number of correct answers and the same number of days played share the same rank.</p><p>The displayed ranking percentage gives 75% weight to correct answers and 25% weight to participation, measured against the number of quiz days available in that period. This percentage is informational; rank order itself is based on correct answers and days played.</p><p>The ranking preference can be changed at any time in Personal Settings.</p>`},'''
new='''rankings:{title:"STATISTICS & RANKINGS",body:`<p><strong>My Statistics</strong> is divided into three periods: <strong>This Week</strong>, <strong>This Month</strong> and <strong>All Time</strong>.</p><p>For each period, your personal statistics show <strong>Played</strong> (the number of quiz questions you submitted), <strong>Correct</strong>, <strong>Incorrect</strong> and <strong>Accuracy</strong> (the percentage of your submitted answers that were correct).</p><p>Each of the three periods has its own <strong>Quiz Top 20</strong>. The weekly Top 20 uses results from the current quiz week, the monthly Top 20 uses results from the current calendar month, and the All-Time Top 20 uses the complete recorded quiz history.</p><p>Participation in the Quiz Top 20 rankings is optional. Results remain private unless the player chooses <strong>INCLUDE ME IN RANKINGS</strong> in Personal Settings. Only players who have opted into rankings are included, and ordinary players can see other players' ranking information only when they also participate in the rankings.</p><p>Quiz rankings are based on quiz performance. Players are ordered first by the number of correct answers and then by the number of different days played during the relevant period. Players with the same number of correct answers and the same number of days played share the same rank.</p><p>The displayed ranking percentage gives 75% weight to correct answers and 25% weight to participation, measured against the number of quiz days available in that period. This percentage is informational; rank order itself is based on correct answers and days played.</p><p><strong>Title statistics are separate from quiz-performance rankings.</strong> The title system records how many times a player has won <strong>Smartest BDL'er of the Week</strong> and <strong>The Supreme BDL'er of The Month</strong>.</p><p>Title Points are calculated as follows: each Smartest win is worth <strong>1 Title Point</strong> and each Supreme win is worth <strong>4 Title Points</strong>. Total Title Points = Smartest wins + (Supreme wins × 4).</p><p>The <strong>Title Top 20</strong> is an <strong>All-Time ranking only</strong>. There is no weekly or monthly Title Top 20. It is shown separately from the Quiz Top 20 and does not change a player's quiz-performance rank.</p><p><strong>Ranking participation does not affect your chances of winning.</strong> Choosing to appear in the rankings, or choosing to keep your results private, has no influence on eligibility or chances of becoming a weekly or monthly winner. Eligible quiz results are considered for winner selection regardless of the ranking privacy setting.</p><p><strong>Test and administrative accounts</strong>, including Amy.test and DrBDL.test, may view the real rankings and relevant statistics in a read-only test/admin view so the quiz can be checked and maintained. This access does not change a player's ranking preference or make private results public to ordinary players. Test accounts remain excluded from the rankings and from weekly and monthly winner selection.</p><p>The ranking preference can be changed at any time in Personal Settings.</p>`},'''
if old not in s: raise SystemExit('ranking policy block not found')
s=s.replace(old,new,1)
s=s.replace("['rankings','RANKING RULES']","['rankings','STATISTICS & RANKINGS']",1)
s=s.replace('<strong>Last updated: 30 August 2026</strong>','<strong>Last updated: 31 August 2026</strong>',1)
p.write_text(s)
